<title>NEW ZEALAND: INP unit picks up 7.56 pct of W&amp;H.</title>
<headline>INP unit picks up 7.56 pct of W&amp;H.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Independent Press Communications Ltd, a subsidiary of Independent Newspapers Plc, said it had so far acquired 7.4 million shares or 7.56 percent in its bid for New Zealand publisher Wilson and Horton.</p>
<p>IPCL is bidding for all of Wilson and Horton, offering NZ$11.00 or 1.375 exchangeable INP shares for each W&amp;H share.</p>
<p>Prior to the bid, Independent Newspapers Plc held 22.6 percent of Wilson and Horton, with the same amount in the hands of family trusts linked to principal Tony O'Reilly.</p>
<p>-- Wellington newsroom 64 4 473-4746</p>
</text>
